Perfect! Frida is now installed and fully accessible inside your virtual environment, running version 17.15.3.
Now you need to make sure the companion tool (frida-server) running on your mobile device or emulator matches this exact version.

Next Steps to Connect

1. Download matching Frida Server:
Go to the Frida GitHub Releases page and download frida-server-17.15.3-android-arm64.xz (or x86_64 if using a standard PC emulator like Genymotion/Android Studio).
2. Push and Run on Device:bash
# Extract the file
unxz frida-server-17.15.3-android-*.xz

# Push to device
adb push frida-server-17.15.3-android-* /data/local/tmp/frida-server

# Execution (on device via adb shell as root)
adb shell
su
chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/frida-server
/data/local/tmp/frida-server &
Use code with caution.
3. Verify the Connection:
Open a new terminal tab (or stay in your current one), ensure your virtual environment is active, and test the connection by listing the processes on your device:bash
frida-ps -U
Use code with caution.
